.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH add 1  "add " 
.SH NAME
add \- Add `value` to the list field `field` of item `id`. The value is trimmed and validated against the field\*(Aqs type — on a `ref` field it is an item id of one of the field\*(Aqs `targets`, and a bare local id is resolved. Adding a value the field already holds does not add a second entry: it gives that entry this label (or none, without `\-\-label`)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBadd\fR [\fB\-\-label\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIID\fR> <\fIFIELD\fR> <\fIVALUE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Add `value` to the list field `field` of item `id`. The value is trimmed and validated against the field\*(Aqs type — on a `ref` field it is an item id of one of the field\*(Aqs `targets`, and a bare local id is resolved. Adding a value the field already holds does not add a second entry: it gives that entry this label (or none, without `\-\-label`)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-label\fR \fI<LABEL>\fR
Label the entry (free text, e.g. `work` or `private`; trimmed, not blank)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIID\fR>

.TP
<\fIFIELD\fR>

.TP
<\fIVALUE\fR>

